## `unit` gate: pre-existing failure on `b7e0122`, resolved on `main` `32c8f28`

The first P4-02 run recorded `unit` as FAIL: `pnpm test` failed only in `@project-air/design-check`
because `tools/design-check/test/design-check.test.mjs` asserted
`checkProject(repoRoot).skipped.length === 0` while the gate reports four informational non-px
"skipped" values (not findings; the CLI exits 0) from `apps/web/preview/preview.css` lines 1016, 1017,
1059, 1060 (`inset-block-start: 50%`, `inset-inline-start: calc(100% + var(--space-8))`) that merged
earlier with P0-24/P0-25/P1-07. Those tasks ran no repo-wide `unit` gate; the same failure reproduces
from an extracted `b7e0122` tree.

The owner-approved main fix `32c8f28` ("allow documented design-check skips in the repo-wide test")
adds the documented skip allowlist and removes the false failure. On the rebased branch (base `main`
`32c8f28`) the gate was rerun and passes: 15/15 turbo tasks successful and every test package green,
including the new `packages/test-kit` scene suite (`12` tests, `pass 12`, `fail 0`). The obsolete
failing record no longer exists in the tree; the authoritative record is
`reviews/evidence/P4-02-unit-20261026T055547Z.json` (log `…-unit-20261026T055547Z.log`).
